      "extract": "For f ∈L∞(R+) ∩L1(R+) consider the Bessel kernel Bf(x, y) = Z R+ t√xyJν(xt)Jν(yt)f(t) dt, (1.1) where Jν is the Bessel function of order ν. Fix ν > −1. The kernel (1.1) induces a bounded linear operator on L2(R+), which we will also denote by Bf. We let B1 be equal to the identity operator. We refer to Bf as the Bessel operator. For any h ∈L∞(X) we also let h denote the operator of pointwise multiplication by this",
      "extractCut": true
