      "extract": "For a function f ∈L1(R) ∩L∞(R) we define its Fourier transform by bf(λ) = 1 2π Z R e−iλxf(x) dx. Here and below, if f is defined on R+, then we extend it to an even function. In this case the Fourier transform coincides with the cosine transform. Recall that the Sobolev p-seminorm of a function f on R+ is ∥f∥2 ˙Hp = Z R+ | bf(λ)|2|λ|2p dλ. For an integer p we have ∥f∥˙Hp = (2π)−1/2∥f (p)∥L2(R+) by Parseval’s",
