      "extract": "and the determinantal point process with Bessel kernel Let E be R or R+ = [0, ∞). Recall that a configuration on E is a discrete subset of E. We denote the set of configurations by Conf(E). It can be endowed with a σ-algebra of measurable subsets X (for instance, see [25]). A point process P is defined to be a probability measure on (Conf(E), X). For a measurable function f : E →C we define two measurable functions",
