      "extract": "Recall that the Wiener–Hopf operator as a map W: f 7→Wf, L∞(R) → B(L2(R+)) is not a Banach algebra homomorphism. But it can be restricted to some subalgebras on which it preserves multiplication. Recall that H1(R) is a Banach algebra. The spaces H± 1 (R) = {f ∈H1(R): supp bf ⊂R±} are Banach subalgebras since supp( bf ∗bg) ⊂supp bf + supp bg. The operators P± = F−1χR±F map H1(R) into itself and P±H1(R) = H± 1 (R).",
